# The interactive Python session of record_replay.sh, typed into python3 -q. It runs under the
# recorder alone, no layer between it and the terminal, so one Ctrl+C reaches Python once. Every step
# waits for something Python prints, never for a time, and markers are printed in two halves so the
# echo of the typed line can never satisfy an expectation.
expect >>>
send import time
send print("OK-" + "P1")
expect OK-P1
send print("OK-" + "P2", flush=True); time.sleep(30)
expect OK-P2
key ctrl-c
expect KeyboardInterrupt
send print("OK-" + "P3")
expect OK-P3
send exit(0)
